      <dico>Lessing</dico>
      <unicode>ᠡᠴᠠ</unicode>
      <uighur>eče</uighur>
      <transcript>ECE</transcript>
      <definition>Suffix of the ablative case with the following functions: a) Separative ablative denoting direction from, moving away from, beginning with, springing from (referring both to space and time). b) Ablative of contact. c) Ablative of cause or reason. d) Partitive ablative ( indicating objects which are only partially affected by the action). e) Exclusive ablative (usually followed by such words as: busu, øger-e, γadana) in constructions corresponding to "besides," "different from," "apart from, " " except," "other than. " f) Comparative ablative. g) Agentive or subjective ablative denoting the actor (actual subject), especially with passive verb forms. h) Objective ablative used with verbs meaning to fear, beg, request.</definition>
      <page>291</page>
